    <string name="rankings_info_title">How rankings work</string>
    <string name="rankings_info_introduction">By default, teams are ranked by series Elo. Explore also lets you rank by map Elo, series played, or win rate. Choosing a circuit selects its teams; their ratings and records still include every circuit. Rankings are in beta and may change as they are tuned.</string>
    <string name="rankings_info_eligibility_title">Who is ranked</string>
    <string name="rankings_info_eligibility_body">Teams need at least 5 rated series in the last 180 days and a match in the last 90 days. These rules apply in both views. All matching teams are shown, up to 50.</string>
    <string name="rankings_info_elo_title">How Elo works</string>
    <string name="rankings_info_elo_body">Elo compares a match result with what the ratings predict. Beating a stronger team earns more points; losing to a weaker team costs more. Expected results usually move ratings less.</string>
    <string name="rankings_info_context_title">Read ratings in context</string>
    <string name="rankings_info_context_body">Teams from different regions and circuits meet less often, so their ratings are linked through fewer matches. Treat small gaps as close, and the W–L record as context for the rating.</string>
    <string name="rankings_info_close">Done</string>
